            <ArticleTitle>Pheochromocytoma and tetralogy of Fallot: Coincidence or a rare association?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>75-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0218492314545499</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 25-year-old woman with tetralogy of Fallot who presented with chest pain and hypertension, and on further investigation, was diagnosed with a pheochromocytoma in the right adrenal gland. She underwent surgical excision of the tumor. While the simultaneous occurrence of these two diseases is extremely rare, the suspicion of a possible relationship has been raised in the past.</AbstractText>
